    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> class designed to allow extending user input in a transparent way. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An input binding, when set to an editor, can intercept all the events the editor receive and radically change the behavior.</para><para>The main purpose of this class is twofold : <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Allow vi-like (or emacs-like, ...) editing to be implemented with little extra work. And allow the user to easily switch between input modes </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Allow applications using <ref refid="namespaceQCE" kindref="compound">QCE</ref> to easily add extra features (e.g extended code navigation within projects, jump to documentation, ...) with little extra work </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
